---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiLandingHero from '../../components/AiLandingHero.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SolutionFaq from '../../components/SolutionFaq.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';

const context = 'AI-assisted public services';
---

<Base
  title="AI for public services | Registry Stack"
  description="Design a service people can try, build it with our team on open-source software, and evaluate guided access through a compatible AI assistant."
>
  <SiteHeader current="ai" />
  <main>
    <AiLandingHero
      eyebrow="AI for public services"
      heading="Design and deliver public services with AI."
      lead="Turn forms and research into a service brief with AI. Build the service with our team in a scoped pilot. Test an experimental integration for starting selected requests in chat."
      context={context}
      exampleHref="#ai-jobs"
      exampleLabel="Explore the three uses"
    >
      <p class="ai-example-label">One registry service</p>
      <p class="ai-example-title">Update a contact address</p>
      <ol class="address-flow" aria-label="Design, implementation and access for an address correction">
        <li><span class="flow-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><span class="ai-example-label">Service design</span><strong>Find out what the applicant needs to provide</strong></div></li>
        <li><span class="flow-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><span class="ai-example-label">Implementation</span><strong>Set who can review and update the address</strong></div></li>
        <li><span class="flow-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><span class="ai-example-label">Citizen access</span><strong>Help the applicant prepare a draft in chat</strong></div></li>
      </ol>
    </AiLandingHero>

    <section class="section" id="ai-jobs" aria-labelledby="jobs-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="jobs-title">Where AI helps your service team</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-job-grid">
          <article>
            <p class="availability">Design method</p>
            <h3>Design a service people can try</h3>
            <p>Use your forms and research to draft a service brief. Test the proposed steps with applicants and staff before committing to a build.</p>
            <a class="inline-cta" href="/ai/service-design/">Explore service design <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </article>
          <article class="pilot">
            <p class="availability">Available through a scoped pilot</p>
            <h3>Build and adapt one service</h3>
            <p>Work with our team to adapt records, forms and review steps. Check the proposed changes against your rules and try them on realistic cases.</p>
            <a class="inline-cta" href="/customization/">Explore implementation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </article>
          <article>
            <p class="availability">Experimental integration</p>
            <h3>Help people start a request in chat</h3>
            <p>Let a signed-in person prepare a correction with an approved assistant. They review and submit the draft on your service website.</p>
            <a class="inline-cta" href="/ai/citizen-access/">Explore citizen access <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="control-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="control-title">Your institution sets the rules</h2>
          <p>Your team approves service changes and decides what each person or connected system can see and do. The registry applies those permissions when it receives a request.</p>
          <a class="inline-cta" href="/architecture/headless/">See how Registry Stack fits behind your interfaces <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-callout">
          <h3>Use the channels that suit your service</h3>
          <p>The configured service can run without an AI model. Keep an existing portal or staff application and add an assistant for a selected task when it fits.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <SolutionFaq
      heading="Planning your first service"
      items={[
        {
          q: 'Can we start with a service we already run?',
          a: 'Yes. Bring the forms and procedures you use today. We can assess what can stay in place and which parts would need configuring or connecting.',
        },
        {
          q: 'What does an implementation pilot cover?',
          a: 'We agree the service, what to test, who operates each part and what your team receives. Pricing and responsibilities depend on the written scope.',
          link: { href: '/pricing/', label: 'See implementation and support options' },
        },
        {
          q: 'Can we evaluate the assistant channel on its own?',
          a: 'You can evaluate it for a selected task on a configured Base Registry Engine service. Start with one correction and agree what the assistant can see and prepare.',
          link: { href: '/ai/citizen-access/', label: 'See the address correction example' },
        },
      ]}
    />

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 id="next-title">Choose one service to improve</h2>
        <p>Bring a form, a process or a request people make often. We’ll discuss what you want to change and what your team can evaluate first.</p>
        <div class="section-links">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">View implementation options</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .address-flow { display: grid; gap: 12px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .address-flow li {
    align-items: start;
    background: var(--registry-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding: 11px 12px;
  }
  .address-flow strong { display: block; font-size: var(--type-body-sm); line-height: 1.35; }
  .flow-number {
    background: var(--registry-blue-tint);
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: var(--registry-blue);
    font: 600 var(--type-sm)/1.4 var(--registry-mono);
    padding: 6px 7px;
  }
  .ai-job-grid { display: grid; gap: 20px; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .ai-job-grid article {
    background: var(--registry-paper-half);
    border: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--registry-blue);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 28px);
  }
  .ai-job-grid .pilot { background: var(--registry-blue-tint); border-color: var(--registry-blue-rule); border-top-color: var(--registry-blue); }
  .ai-job-grid h3 { font-size: var(--type-xl); }
  .ai-job-grid .inline-cta { align-self: start; margin-top: auto; }
  .availability {
    color: var(--registry-blue);
    font: 600 var(--type-xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .ai-job-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>
